  "footnotes": [],
  "context": "The budget of the local expenses funds for 1918 (revenue and expenditure each 5,894,000 yen), by province and compared with 1910-1917, shows the taxes, subsidies and other revenue by which provinces meet local outlays for education, public works, sanitation and industry.",
  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Rows: 13 provinces + Total + 8 years (1917-1910) in each of the four parts as printed; the printed Total row is placed after the provinces and the year rows follow, as in the original. Dashes in the original written as '...'.",
   "Part A (printed p. 155 with 1917-1910 rows on p. 156 under '(Continued)') read from crops of full/p0191.jpg and full/p0192.jpg; part B from full/p0192.jpg; part C from full/p0193.jpg; part D from full/p0194.jpg.",
   "Part A: all six tax columns and the Total column sum to the printed Total row (537,992; 17,313; 599,724; 297,478; 236,879; 286,833; 1,976,219). Province rows sum to their printed totals.",
   "Part A year rows: 1917, 1916, 1913, 1911 reconcile; 1915 parts sum 1,462,211 vs printed 1,462,210; 1914 parts sum 1,284,291 vs printed 1,284,289; 1912 parts sum 901,484 vs printed 901,481 (kept as printed). Row 1910, Total: printed figure damaged ('1 0?0,715'): '[?]'.",
   "Part B: columns Receipts from Imperial Donation Funds, Balance, Subsidy and Other Sources sum to the printed Total row; printed Total row sums (taxes total 1,976,219 + 4 columns) to 5,894,402. Each province's printed total equals its Part A total plus its four Part B figures where readable.",
   "Part B unreadable (smudged/damaged print): South Zenra, Total; South Heian, Total (both legible in part D as 533,333 and 553,295, but not used here). South Keishō, Total: last digit unclear between 3/8/6 in the heavy type ('500,69?'); neither 3 nor 8 fits the sum (500,696), so '[?]'.",
   "Part B year rows: 1914 parts sum 2,930,761 vs printed 2,930,762 (kept as printed); 1913 parts sum 2,697,557 vs printed 2,697,556 (kept as printed); other years reconcile with part A year total + part B columns where part A total readable (1910 not checkable: part A total unreadable).",
   "Part C (Expenditure): Sanitation, Industrial Encouragement and Livelihood column sums equal the printed Total row; Civil Engineering sums to 1,536,988 vs printed 1,536,992; Relief and Charity sums to 103,744 (with South Heian read as [?] counted as 0) vs printed 103,753. South Heian, Relief and Charity: last digit damaged ('7,05?'): '[?]'.",
   "Part D: all columns sum to the printed Total row except Total column 5,894,401 vs printed 5,894,402 (13 province rows as printed). Province row totals reconcile with parts C + D except South Keishō (parts 500,692 vs printed 500,695; the final digit of the printed total is in heavy type, read as 5) and South Heian (parts, with Relief [?] counted as 0: 553,286 vs printed 553,295). Year rows 1917-1910 reconcile in total with C + D.",
   "The printed Total (Part C Total row) civil engineering etc. figures: Total row C: 1,536,992; 196,515; 103,753; 1,050,719; 894,856; Part D Total row 5,894,402 equals revenue total.",
   "Part C and D totals for years: Part C year rows have '—' in Affording Means of Livelihood for 1916-1910 (written '...').",
   "1910 Total (part 1) 1,000,715 (first reading unreadable; an independent second reading and a third reader agree).",
   "Verified: an independent blind second transcription agreed on every figure except the cells noted; totals that do not reconcile are as printed."
  ],
